{"format":"vetro-plugin","version":1,"manifest":{"id":"elm-leak-fix","name":"EFL leak fix","version":"1.0.0","apiVersion":1,"permissions":["exec"],"main":"index.js","ui":{"label":"Leak fix"},"description":"Stops msf-server rewriting the Elementary config every second (pw-show-lastset), which leaks memory in every EFL app and freezes the UI.","author":"elmasevmem"},"files":{"README.md":"# EFL leak fix\n\nA Vetro Shard that stops a memory leak in Samsung's firmware which makes the TV's UI freeze after a few hours:\nthe menu, volume overlay and remote stop answering while the picture and sound keep playing, until the TV is\nrestarted with a long press on the power button.\n\n## Why\n\nOn some firmware `msf-server` (Samsung's Multiscreen / SmartThings remote server) runs `/usr/bin/pw-show-lastset 1`\n**every second**, even with no phone connected. That helper only saves the Elementary \"show the last character of a\npassword\" setting, so each run rewrites `~/share/.elementary/config/tv/base.cfg` with the same content. Every EFL app\nwatches that file: on each write tv-viewer, menu, YouTube, ScreenMirroring, registertv, qdinfo-daemon and others\nreload their config and fonts and leak heap. On a Q70A that was about 2.4 MB per minute per app, roughly 26 MB per\nminute in total; once RAM and swap run out the UI freezes.\n\nHow to see whether your TV has it (Shell Shard or SSH):\n\n```sh\nstat -c %y /opt/usr/home/owner/share/.elementary/config/tv/base.cfg   # run twice a few seconds apart: changes every second\nps -eo pid,ppid,args | grep pw-show-lastset                             # spawned again and again by msf-server\n```\n\nThe Shard binds `/bin/true` over `/usr/bin/pw-show-lastset` in the init mount namespace. msf-server keeps running\n(phone remote, Smart View and SmartThings still work); the helper simply does nothing. The only thing lost is that\na phone can no longer change the \"show last password character\" setting. Nothing on the TV's storage is changed:\na bind mount disappears at reboot, which is why the Shard applies it again after every boot.\n\n## Permissions\n\n`exec`: the bind mount is a root command, run through the TV's root agent.\n\n## Commands it runs\n\n| Command | Why |\n| --- | --- |\n| `[ -e /usr/bin/pw-show-lastset ] && ! grep -q \" /usr/bin/pw-show-lastset \" /proc/1/mountinfo && nsenter -t 1 -m mount --bind /bin/true /usr/bin/pw-show-lastset`, then the check below | applies the fix in the init mount namespace (where msf-server runs), only if the helper exists and is not bound yet |\n| `if [ ! -e /usr/bin/pw-show-lastset ]; then echo absent; elif grep -q \" /usr/bin/pw-show-lastset \" /proc/1/mountinfo; then echo bound; else echo free; fi` | reads back whether the fix is in place |\n| `nsenter -t 1 -m umount /usr/bin/pw-show-lastset` (up to 5 times while it is still bound), then the check | removes the fix when the Shard is switched off |\n\nWhen: 2 s after the Shard starts, then every 15 s until the root agent answers (it is not up for the first minute or\ntwo after a boot; at most 80 tries, then every 10 minutes), then every 10 minutes to put the bind back if something\nremoved it. **Check now** on the page runs the apply command once. Switching the Shard off runs the remove command.\nOn firmware without the helper it reports `not needed` and only looks again every 10 minutes.\n\n## Network\n\nNone. The page talks only to its own routes (`state`, `check`).\n\n## Data it keeps\n\nNone. It does not use `ctx.config`.\n\n## Tested on\n\nSamsung QE65Q70A (2021), Tizen 6.0, firmware T-NKM2DEUC, Vetro 0.7.0:\n\n- before: `base.cfg` was rewritten every second and `MemAvailable` dropped by about 70 MB every 3 minutes\n  (1066 MB to 770 MB in 15 minutes after a boot); the UI froze after a few hours.\n- with the bind in place: `base.cfg` no longer changes, the heap of tv-viewer, menu, YouTube, registertv and\n  qdinfo-daemon stays flat, and `MemAvailable` stays level (1133 MB to 1137 MB over 40 s, 6 minutes after a boot).\n- after a reboot the Shard applied the bind on its own once the root agent answered.\n\n## Install\n\nFrom the Shard catalog in **Vetro Shards**, or from a file: download the `.vplugin`, then\n**Vetro Shards → Install from a file or develop a Shard** (needs Developer mode). It installs switched off; switch it on.\n","index.js":"'use strict';\n// EFL leak fix: a Vetro Shard. Plain ES5: older TVs run Node 4.4.\n//\n// On some Samsung firmware msf-server (the Multiscreen / SmartThings remote server) spawns\n// /usr/bin/pw-show-lastset every second. Each run saves the Elementary config\n// (~/share/.elementary/config/tv/base.cfg) with the same content, every EFL app on the TV\n// (tv-viewer, menu, YouTube, ScreenMirroring, ...) reloads its config and fonts and leaks heap,\n// and after a few hours the UI stops answering while video and sound keep playing.\n//\n// The fix binds /bin/true over the helper in the init mount namespace, so msf-server still runs\n// but the helper does nothing. A bind mount does not survive a reboot, so the Shard applies it\n// once the root agent answers and checks it every 10 minutes. Switching it off removes the bind.\n\nvar TARGET = '/usr/bin/pw-show-lastset';\nvar BOUND = 'grep -q \" ' + TARGET + ' \" /proc/1/mountinfo';\nvar CHECK = 'if [ ! -e ' + TARGET + ' ]; then echo absent; elif ' + BOUND + '; then echo bound; else echo free; fi';\nvar APPLY = '[ -e ' + TARGET + ' ] && ! ' + BOUND + ' && nsenter -t 1 -m mount --bind /bin/true ' + TARGET + '; ' + CHECK;\nvar UNDO = 'n=0; while ' + BOUND + ' && [ $n -lt 5 ]; do nsenter -t 1 -m umount ' + TARGET + ' || break; n=$((n+1)); done; ' + CHECK;\n\nvar RETRY_MS = 15000, RETRY_MAX = 80, CHECK_MS = 600000;\n\nmodule.exports = function (ctx) {\n    var timer = null, tries = 0, busy = false, running = false;\n    var st = { state: 'idle', result: null, lastCheck: null, lastError: null };\n\n    function run(cmd) {\n        return ctx.execute(cmd, 15000).then(function (r) {\n            var out = String(r && r.stdout || '').trim();\n            if (r && (r.exit_code || r.timed_out)) throw new Error(String(r && r.stderr || out || 'command failed').trim());\n            return out.split('\\n').pop();\n        });\n    }\n\n    function schedule(ms) {\n        if (timer) clearTimeout(timer);\n        timer = null;\n        if (!running) return;\n        timer = setTimeout(tick, ms);\n        if (timer.unref) timer.unref();\n    }\n\n    function record(out) {\n        st.result = out; st.lastCheck = new Date().toISOString();\n    }\n\n    function tick() {\n        timer = null;\n        if (!running) return;\n        if (busy) { schedule(RETRY_MS); return; }\n        busy = true;\n        run(APPLY).then(function (out) {\n            record(out);\n            if (out === 'bound') {\n                st.state = 'active'; st.lastError = null; tries = 0;\n                schedule(CHECK_MS);\n            } else if (out === 'absent') {\n                // This firmware has no helper: nothing to do, look again later (an update may add it).\n                st.state = 'not needed'; st.lastError = null; tries = 0;\n                schedule(CHECK_MS);\n            } else {\n                throw new Error('Bind is not in place (' + out + ')');\n            }\n        }).catch(function (e) {\n            st.lastError = String(e && e.message || e);\n            // The root agent does not answer for the first minute or two after a boot.\n            if (++tries <= RETRY_MAX) { st.state = 'waiting'; schedule(RETRY_MS); }\n            else { st.state = 'failed'; tries = 0; schedule(CHECK_MS); }\n        }).then(function () { busy = false; });\n    }\n\n    function json(res, body, code) {\n        res.writeHead(code || 200, { 'content-type': 'application/json', 'cache-control': 'no-store' });\n        res.end(JSON.stringify(body));\n    }\n\n    var PAGE = '<!doctype html><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"color-scheme\" content=\"light dark\">' +\n        '<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\">' +\n        '<style>body{font:16px system-ui;margin:24px;max-width:40em}pre{white-space:pre-wrap}' +\n        'button{font:inherit;padding:10px 20px;border-radius:8px}</style>' +\n        '<h2>EFL leak fix</h2>' +\n        '<p>Keeps <code>' + TARGET + '</code> switched off, so msf-server stops rewriting the Elementary ' +\n        'config every second and the TV apps stop leaking memory. <b>active</b> means the fix is in place; ' +\n        '<b>not needed</b> means this firmware has no such helper.</p>' +\n        '<pre id=\"s\">Reading…</pre><button id=\"b\">Check now</button><script>' +\n        'var s=document.getElementById(\"s\");' +\n        'function show(d){s.textContent=JSON.stringify(d,null,2)}' +\n        'function get(){fetch(\"state\").then(function(r){return r.json()}).then(show).catch(function(){s.textContent=\"No answer\"})}' +\n        'document.getElementById(\"b\").onclick=function(){s.textContent=\"Checking…\";' +\n        'fetch(\"check\",{method:\"POST\",headers:{\"Content-Type\":\"application/json\"},body:\"{}\"}).then(function(r){return r.json()}).then(show).catch(function(){s.textContent=\"Request failed\"})};' +\n        'get();</script>';\n\n    return {\n        start: function () { running = true; tries = 0; st.state = 'waiting'; schedule(2000); },\n        stop: function () {\n            running = false;\n            if (timer) { clearTimeout(timer); timer = null; }\n            st.state = 'off';\n            return run(UNDO).then(record, function () {});\n        },\n        status: function () { return { state: st.state, result: st.result, lastCheck: st.lastCheck, lastError: st.lastError }; },\n        route: function (req, res, sub) {\n            if (sub === 'ui' && req.method === 'GET') {\n                res.writeHead(200, { 'content-type': 'text/html; charset=utf-8', 'cache-control': 'no-store' });\n                res.end(PAGE);\n                return true;\n            }\n            if (sub === 'state' && req.method === 'GET') { json(res, st); return true; }\n            if (sub === 'check' && req.method === 'POST') {\n                if (!running) { json(res, st); return true; }\n                run(APPLY).then(function (out) {\n                    record(out);\n                    if (out === 'bound') { st.state = 'active'; st.lastError = null; }\n                    else if (out === 'absent') st.state = 'not needed';\n                    json(res, st);\n                }, function (e) { st.lastError = String(e && e.message || e); json(res, st, 503); });\n                return true;\n            }\n            return false;\n        }\n    };\n};\n"}}
